 vibes about  it mixed with studio ghibli an element  of the magical doorknob still made it  into the final film though when at the  end antonio gives mirabelle a doorknob  with her initial on it which she uses to  bring the reconstructed cassita back to  magical life bad casita initial concepts  for the magical house also gave it a  more mischievous personality and it was  even antagonistic towards mirabelle to  begin with bad casita initially tried to  stop mirabelle on her quest for example  there was this moment when the house  sent her shooting up into the sky  another moment where it looks like it  blocked her way through a door by  putting another door in her way and then  there was this scene where it appears to  have flooded her bedroom and in another  spooky unused scene family members  discover cassita is spying on their  private conversation about how they  think the house is crazy and in this  zany test animation mirabelle had to  compete with cassita for abuela's  approval while the house deliberately  sabotaged her efforts to please her  grandmother  funhouse casita and encanto almost had  an additional mind-bending sci-fi-ish  element blended with its magical realism  giving it shades of doctor strange or  inception where casita would have turned  itself into a fun house creating these  weird slanting disorienting corridors  and doorways that folded in on  themselves this idea also reminds me of  these trippy visuals in the third  country movie the devil made me do it  space spending casita in another  strangely entertaining version of casita  the space in the house would have made  even less logical sense for example in  this unused concept art mirabelle could  hide in this cabinet over on the left  but her arm would be able to emerge  magically through this cupboard on the  right so she could sneak a pastry or two  with a bell's deep dive and in another  unused casita storyline there was a vast  underwater world beneath the house that  mirabelle had to explore which i suspect  was part of her original quest  magical wallpaper in the end the  filmmakers opted to make casita a much  friendlier character and we can see that  change in this unused concept art where  the house helped mirabelle by folding  pieces of wallpaper into magical birds  that would guide her on a mission to  discover the mystery of the encanto in  some other art it also appears the  wallpaper could act as a portal or door  to a magical world behind the walls in  this art a door seems to open up an  isabella's bedroom wall to a place where  she could relax and be happy then  there's this unused art which shows how  originally cassita's mood was going to  reflect mirabelle's mood for example  here you can see the wallpaper crying  while mirabella feels sad at being left  out of the family fun and the house also  joined in on reenactments of historical  battles with isabella's magical potato  people more on that later  coffee with cassita i love this idea of  mirabelle sharing a morning coffee with  the magical house and putting hats on  the chairs and lamp the casita  communicated through we got a little  touch of this rejected idea in the final  movie when cassita pours coffee for the  family  luisa holds up the sky it's a shame we  didn't get to see inside luisa's room  because there were some very cool ideas  for how it would look for instance the  room would have had several large  boulders that fell from above and luisa  had to keep them up with her feet that  idea was intended to be reminiscent of  the myth of atlas carrying the sky most  of the things in the room appear to be  made of rocks including the stone bed  but one especially sweet contrasting  detail is the little puppy louisa holds  and there's some more cute concept art  of luisa with puppies here  jungle furniture as impressive as  antonio's room is in the movie an early  idea had an even more surreal design for  example the furniture inside had merged  with parts of the ra